@startuml 06-module-map
!include _theme.iuml

title The packages under src/pyvider/cty, and which way the imports actually point

skinparam nodesep 18
skinparam ranksep 32
skinparam rectangleFontSize 12

rectangle "**functions/**   //the top of the library//\nthe framework: _function.py — CtyFunction, CtyFunctionSpec,\nCtyParameter, RefineResult · _args · _marks · _unknowns · _framework\nthe stdlib: 83 functions over bool, bytes, collection, comparison,\nconversion, datetime, encoding, format, numeric, set, string, structural" as FUNCS <<core>>

rectangle "**pyvider.cty**   //the public surface//\nre-exports the types, CtyValue, convert and unify, both codecs,\nthe parser, refine, the mark and path helpers, walk, conformance" as ROOT <<core>>

rectangle "**the wire modules**\ncodec.py — msgpack\njson_codec.py — cty/json" as WIRE <<capsule>>

rectangle "**the value-level modules**\nmarks.py · mark_paths.py · walk.py · unknown.py\nvalue_range.py · conformance.py · refinement.py\nparser.py · graphemes.py" as VMODS <<capsule>>

rectangle "**conversion/**\nexplicit — convert, can_convert_unsafe\nunify · raw_to_cty · adapter\ntype_encoder · inference_cache" as CONV <<plumbing>>

rectangle "**types/**\nbase · primitives · collections\nstructural · capsule" as TYPES <<structural>>

rectangle "**path/**\nCtyPath · GetAttrStep\nIndexStep · KeyStep" as PATH <<structural>>

rectangle "**validation/**\nrecursion — the guard\nmarks — preserves_marks" as VALID <<collection>>

rectangle "**values/**\nbase — CtyValue\nmarkers — UnknownValue, RefinedUnknownValue\nequality · frozen" as VALUES <<primitive>>

rectangle "**exceptions/**\nbase · validation · conversion · encoding\n//no runtime cty imports at all//" as EXC <<plumbing>>
rectangle "**config/**\ndefaults · runtime\n//every constant lives here//" as CONFIG <<plumbing>>
rectangle "**_unicode/**\ncase · grapheme\n+ generated tables" as UNI <<plumbing>>
rectangle "**context/**\nvalidation_context" as CTX <<plumbing>>

FUNCS --> ROOT
ROOT --> WIRE
ROOT --> VMODS
ROOT --> CONV
ROOT --> TYPES
ROOT --> VALUES

WIRE --> CONV
WIRE --> VMODS
WIRE --> TYPES
WIRE --> VALUES

VMODS --> TYPES
VMODS --> VALUES
VMODS --> PATH
VMODS --> UNI

CONV --> TYPES
CONV --> VALUES
CONV --> EXC
CONV --> CONFIG

TYPES --> VALID
TYPES --> VALUES
TYPES --> EXC
TYPES -[#C08787]-> PATH
PATH -[#C08787]-> TYPES
TYPES -[#C08787]-> CONV

PATH --> VALUES
PATH --> EXC
VALUES --> CONFIG
VALID --> CONFIG
CTX --> CONFIG
VALUES -[#98A0B0,dashed]-> TYPES

note left of VALUES
  **values sits below types, and that is deliberate.**
  values/ imports types/ **nowhere** at module scope —
  only under TYPE_CHECKING, and from inside 21
  function bodies. types/ imports values/ at module
  scope and freely. The dashed edge is the lazy
  direction, and CtyValue's own source says why:
  "base.py keeps CtyValue as a TYPE_CHECKING-only
  forward reference to avoid an import cycle, so the
  name does not exist at runtime."
end note

note right of PATH
  **Two module-scope cycles do exist**, drawn in red.
  types/ imports path/ from list, map, object and
  tuple — for the CtyPath in a validation error —
  while path/base.py imports CtyType and CtyValue
  straight back. Separately, types/structural/
  object.py imports conversion/_utils while
  conversion imports types wholesale.
  ----
  Both survive because the types package binds
  CtyType before it imports the subpackages that
  reach back. Every subpackage still imports cleanly
  as an entry point on its own — checked, one fresh
  interpreter each.
end note

note right of FUNCS
  **functions/ is the only package that imports from**
  **the package root**, and it does so 11 times.
  Everything else imports the specific module it
  needs. That is the layering rule the code actually
  obeys: the stdlib sits on top of the whole library,
  and nothing sits on top of the stdlib.
end note

legend bottom
  |= |= reading the arrows |
  | **solid** | a module-scope import, taken at load time — the arrow points the way the dependency runs. |
  | **dashed grey** | reached only under TYPE_CHECKING, or from inside a function body. No load-time dependency. |
  | **red** | a module-scope cycle between two packages. |
  | | The two group boxes — the wire modules, the value-level modules — are top-level .py files\nrather than packages, collected so the graph stays about packages; their arrows are the union of\nthe group's real imports. Everything here came from the AST of every file under src/pyvider/cty,\nnot from the docstrings, counting TYPE_CHECKING and function-local imports separately. |
endlegend

@enduml
